                "content": "# SAN JOAQUIN RIVER BASIN\n\n# 11271290 MERCED RIVER AT SHAFFER BRIDGE, NEAR CRESSEY, CA\n\nLOCATION. Lat 37\u00b027'15\", long 120\u00b036'28\" in NW&SW's sec. 36, T. 5 S., R.12 E., Merced County, near center of span on downstream side of county road bridge, 0.6 mi (1.0 km) upstream from Dry Creek, and 4.0 mi (6.4 km) north- east of Cressey.\n\nDRAINAGE AREA. -1,117 mi \u00b2 (2,893 km2).\n\nPERIOD OF RECORD.--October 1965 to current year (low flow only).\n\nGAGE .--Water-stage recorder. Datum of gage is 116.79 ft (35.598 m) above mean sea level.\n\nREMARKS. --Records fair. Most water released from Lake McClure (stations 11269500, 11270900) is diverted upstream into the Main Canal of Merced Irrigation District. Flow past station consists of releases from diversion dam, irrigation return flow, and tributary inflow. No records computed above 200 ft s/s (5.66 m3/s).\n\nDISCHARGE, IN CUBIC FEET PER SECOND, WATER YEAR OCTOBER 1975 TO SEPTEMBER 1976 MEAN VALUES",
